---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Learning Resources | The Cost of Quality">
	<main class="container">
		<header>
			<h1>Learning Resources</h1>
			<p>A curated collection of archives, theoretical foundations, and datasets for further exploration.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="resource-sections">
			<section class="resource-block">
				<h2>🏛️ Historical Archives & Legislation</h2>
				<ul class="link-list">
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.parliament.uk/about/living-heritage/transformingsociety/livinglearning/19thcentury/overview/factoryact/" target="_blank">
							<strong>UK Parliament: The 1833 Factory Act</strong>
							<span>Official overview of the landmark legislation and its impact.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/education/resources/1833-factory-act/" target="_blank">
							<strong>The National Archives: Education Resources</strong>
							<span>Primary sources and classroom materials on Victorian labor conditions.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="resource-block">
				<h2>🧬 Theoretical Foundations</h2>
				<ul class="link-list">
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.brown.edu/Departments/Economics/Faculty/Oded_Galor/UGT/index.html" target="_blank">
							<strong>Unified Growth Theory (Oded Galor)</strong>
							<span>The comprehensive framework for the transition from Malthusian stagnation to sustained growth.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/1827014" target="_blank">
							<strong>Gary Becker: The Q-Q Tradeoff</strong>
							<span>The seminal 1973 paper: "On the Interaction between the Quantity and Quality of Children."</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="resource-block">
				<h2>📊 Data & Mapping Resources</h2>
				<ul class="link-list">
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.populationspast.org/" target="_blank">
							<strong>Populations Past</strong>
							<span>The primary source for Victorian census data and regional mapping in England and Wales.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
					<li>
						<a href="https://www.hgis.org.uk/" target="_blank">
							<strong>Historical GIS (GBHGIS)</strong>
							<span>Resources for historical administrative boundaries and spatial demographic data.</span>
						</a>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</div>

		<section class="monograph">
			<h2>Open Science Replication Kit</h2>
			<div class="replication-box">
				<p>To ensure full transparency and reproducibility at the University of Copenhagen, the following materials are provided for independent verification:</p>
				<ul class="repro-list">
					<li><input type="checkbox" checked disabled> <strong>Raw Data</strong>: Registration District level transcripts (1851-1881).</li>
					<li><input type="checkbox" checked disabled> <strong>OCR Pipeline</strong>: Python scripts for tabular extraction from PDF archives.</li>
					<li><input type="checkbox" checked disabled> <strong>Harmonization</strong>: Geographic cross-walks for unit boundary changes.</li>
					<li><input type="checkbox" checked disabled> <strong>Codebase</strong>: Final DiD regression logic and robustness tests.</li>
				</ul>
				<div class="repo-links">
					<a href="https://github.com/AntonEbsen/Demography/tree/main/exam_project/data" class="btn secondary">Raw Data Folder</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/AntonEbsen/Demography/tree/main/exam_project/notebooks" class="btn secondary">Analysis Scripts</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.container {
		max-width: 900px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 4rem 2rem;
	}
	header {
		margin-bottom: 5rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: 4rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.resource-sections {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 4rem;
	}
	h2 {
		font-family: var(--serif);
		color: var(--accent);
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.2);
		padding-bottom: 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}
	.link-list {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}
	.link-list li a {
		display: block;
		padding: 2rem;
		background: var(--secondary);
		border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);
		border-radius: 8px;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: inherit;
		transition: all 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
	}
	.link-list li a:hover {
		transform: translateY(-5px);
		border-color: var(--accent);
		background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);
	}
	.link-list li strong {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--serif);
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		color: var(--accent);
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
	.link-list li span {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		opacity: 0.7;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

    .replication-box {
        background: var(--secondary);
        padding: 2.5rem;
        border-radius: 8px;
        border: 1px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.1);
        margin: 2rem 0;
    }
    .repro-list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
        margin: 2rem 0;
    }
    .repro-list li {
        margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
        display: flex;
        gap: 0.8rem;
        align-items: center;
        opacity: 0.8;
    }
    .repro-list input {
        accent-color: var(--accent);
    }
    .repo-links {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1rem;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .monograph h2 {
        font-size: 2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.3);
        padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
        margin: 4rem 0 2rem 0;
    }
</style>
